        {
          "title": "Following",
          "subtitle": "Patience",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Following is a one-deck patience where card placement must follow a fixed rotation of suits."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Following was first described in 1892 in Mary Whitmore Jones Games of Patience. Its name comes from the rule that the player must follow a rotating sequence of suits."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
